@host = http://localhost:8088
@agent = weekend-concierge-approval

# For the deployed agent, get a token with:
# az account get-access-token --scope https://ai.azure.com/.default --query accessToken --output tsv
@endpoint = https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>
@token = <paste the token here>

### 1. Ask for a booking. Dining usually asks for the city and date first
POST {{host}}/responses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Book The Domain Kitchen for 2 people at 7pm on Saturday.",
  "stream": false
}

### 2. Answer it. This response carries the mcp_approval_request items (two of them, for one tool call)
POST {{host}}/responses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "previous_response_id": "<the caresp_... id of the response above>",
  "stream": false,
  "input": "Auckland, and the date is 2026-09-26."
}

### 3. Approve. previous_response_id is the caresp_... id, approval_request_id is the mcpr_... item id
POST {{host}}/responses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "previous_response_id": "<the caresp_... id of the response above>",
  "stream": false,
  "input": [
    {
      "type": "mcp_approval_response",
      "approval_request_id": "<first mcpr_... id>",
      "approve": true
    },
    {
      "type": "mcp_approval_response",
      "approval_request_id": "<second mcpr_... id>",
      "approve": true
    }
  ]
}

### 4. Deployed: ask for a booking
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version=v1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Book The Domain Kitchen for 2 people at 7pm on Saturday.",
  "stream": false
}

### 5. Deployed: answer the city and date, this response carries the mcp_approval_request items
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version=v1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "previous_response_id": "<the caresp_... id of the response above>",
  "stream": false,
  "input": "Auckland, and the date is 2026-09-26."
}

### 6. Deployed: approve. Returns HTTP 200 with "status": "failed", and the booking still happens
POST {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}/endpoint/protocols/openai/responses?api-version=v1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "previous_response_id": "<the caresp_... id of the response above>",
  "stream": false,
  "input": [
    {
      "type": "mcp_approval_response",
      "approval_request_id": "<first mcpr_... id>",
      "approve": true
    },
    {
      "type": "mcp_approval_response",
      "approval_request_id": "<second mcpr_... id>",
      "approve": true
    }
  ]
}

### Delete the agent, its versions, and any active sessions
DELETE {{endpoint}}/agents/{{agent}}?api-version=v1&force=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
